  "annotations": [
   {
    "id": "a1",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "**Airframe.** RigidBody3D on its principal axes (the product of inertia Jxz tilts them 1.16 deg from the body x axis); the air and engine wrench (BeaverWrench) is a modulated source on the body, applied in the geometric body frame through the Mount.",
    "x": 0,
    "y": -100,
    "w": 900,
    "h": 50,
    "color": "blue"
   },
   {
    "id": "a2",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "**Drivetrain (bond graph, our addition).** 1-junction Crank: engine torque P(pz, n, rho)/w (MSe), crank + propeller inertia I = 12 kg m^2, the propeller's torque -Q (MSe) from the governor of the constant-speed propeller, tachometer (SpeedSensor, which makes the bond graph rotational). Global `drivetrain`: 1 the thrust comes from the shaft power Q w, 0 from the source's algebraic power at the commanded rpm (exact FDC).",
    "x": 360,
    "y": 820,
    "w": 900,
    "h": 60,
    "color": "blue"
   }
  ]
